n_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Dastyari","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10819","person_slug":"sam-dastyari","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Skye Kakoschke-Moore","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10854","person_slug":"skye-kakoschke-moore","vote":"no"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Deputy Leader of the Nationals - Senator Nash","noes":32,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2017-09-14.35.1) in respect to Nationals Senator [Fiona Nash](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/fiona_nash), whose eligibility to be a Senator was referred to the Court of Disputed Returns, which means the motion failed. ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(a) notes that the Senate has referred a question as to the eligibility of the Minister for Regional Development (Senator Nash) to serve as a senator to the Court of Disputed Returns for resolution; and* > *(b) resolves that until that question of eligibility has been resolved, Senator Nash shall not exercise the following procedural rights provided to executive senators by the standing orders:* >> *(i) move a motion connected with the conduct of the business of the Senate at any time without notice,* >> *(ii) move that a bill be declared urgent and, if the motion is agreed to, move further motions concerning the time allocated for consideration of the bill,* >> *(iii) move at any time that the Senate adjourn,* >> *(iv) move for the adjournment of debate, having spoken in the debate,* >> *(v) move that the question be now put on more than one occasion, and after having spoken in the debate, and* >> *(vi) present documents.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4923","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2017-09-14/2"}
